## Two direct answers to the framing

1. Recovering the sieve **will not prove JC2** — measured: survivors grow with the divisor structure of `D` through 200, no tail empties. So Q3(f) is answered *yes*, and a uniform theorem must use a datum outside the skeleton.
2. That datum: `d/dx Σ_i f(x,τ_i)^k = J·k·[y^{n-1}](f^{k-1} mod (g−c_2))`, whose left side is `O(k·N) = O(k)` because the boundary pinned `N` to O(1), while the right side is generically `Θ(k·m)`. Verified exactly on 3 Keller pairs, 10 instances, 0 failures. That is the cofinal invariant Q3(a) asks for, and PIN-NOT-CEILING does not forbid it.

